876
00:32:18,900 --> 00:32:20,400
-But I can replace
this overnight.

877
00:32:20,400 --> 00:32:22,410
-You can't replace
the story cell.

878
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:23,900
Without it the
apparatus is useless.

879
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:25,400
-I think it's only shorting.

880
00:32:25,410 --> 00:32:27,910
-Shut up, and get orange hair.

881
00:32:27,910 --> 00:32:29,410
-What if you're right?

882
00:32:29,410 --> 00:32:30,410
Then we can recharge it.

883
00:32:30,410 --> 00:32:31,910
-I'm darn sure we can.

884
00:32:31,910 --> 00:32:33,420
-How long is Lembach staying?

885
00:32:33,410 --> 00:32:35,410
-I'll find out.
-The tension!

886
00:32:35,420 --> 00:32:36,420
How long is Lembach staying?

887
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:38,920
-I'm afraid this takes
precedence over dinner.

888
00:32:38,920 --> 00:32:40,420
-You see, I love Lembach.

889
00:32:40,920 --> 00:32:42,930
-Chris, what does it mean?

890
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:45,920
Well, the idea that somebody
would want to destroy Paul's

891
00:32:45,930 --> 00:32:48,430
discovery, well,
it frightens me.

892
00:32:48,430 --> 00:32:49,930
-Well, if that was
their intention,

893
00:32:49,930 --> 00:32:51,930
